<title>SWEDEN: S-E-Banken posts 5.87 bln skr '96 profit.</title>
<headline>S-E-Banken posts 5.87 bln skr '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings for Swedish bank S-E-Banken in 1996, reported on Friday.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after credit losses	  5,870   vs 3,486</p>
<p> Net interest income		   7,576   vs 6,286</p>
<p> Loan losses			     1,105   vs 3,245</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	   8.91  vs 4.80</p>
<p> Dividend				    2.75  vs 1.50</p>
<p> Commission receivable		 5,543   vs  4,560</p>
<p> Commission payable			844   vs   360</p>
<p> Total income			   17,814   vs 17,078  Total</p>
<p> costs				    10,641   vs  9,567</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	   7,173   vs  7,511</p>
<p> Total capital ratio (pct)	    12.7   vs 15.2</p>
<p> Return on equity (pct)		 22.7   vs 10.7*</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll of 13 analysts showed expectations averaged operating profit after credit losses of 5.68 billion crowns. *Result for the year in relation to average equity.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
